From 73edca8266b3458cfe7f0c39eb90a09d6992229f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Pulipaka <adipu@utexas.edu>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:49:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] Flex filter and SAP sorts/scans on the device (Metal):
 bitonic per world, two-level scan

Warp's radix/segmented sort and scan run on the host on Metal (recorded host calls in the graph). Measured on
the CPU at the sizes of 4096 worlds of a 10x10 cloth + cable: segmented sort of the SAP projections 172 ms,
radix sort of 2.8 M filter keys 25 ms, per step. Now: candidates bucketed by world, each world's segment sorted by
a bitonic network on (key, candidate index) (equal keys keep candidate order, which within an element is
MuJoCo C's generation order), gathered world-major (= the global sort's result); the SAP's per-world rows sorted
the same way; scans in two device levels. FLEX_DEVICE_SORT (None = all but CUDA) selects the path; contact
selections are identical to the host sorts (fidelity harness: same sets and errors).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mujoco_warp/_src/collision_flex.py | 260 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
